# PART A — FINDINGS FROM THE REVERSE-ENGINEERING ANALYSIS

All measurements below are **estimates** from a scaled full-page screenshot (approx. 500px wide render of a ~1440px desktop page, so multiply visual sizes by ~2.9). They are not verified source CSS. Content (copy, links, FAQ, cities, testimonials) was verified against the live site on 5 Nov 2026.

## A. Layout structure
- Page is a single long column of full-width bands; content inside is centred in a constrained container (est. 1200–1280px max; hero and services feel closer to 1200, FAQ is a narrow ~760px column, final CTA panel ~900–1000px).
- Hero: two columns (~55% text / ~45% image). The professional's cutout is large, bleeds to the right edge and sits on a soft mint wash that fades to white at lower-left.
- Alternating background rhythm: white (hero) → white (press strip, with hairline top/bottom border) → light grey #F9FAFC (Why us) → white (services) → near-black (How it works) → white (testimonials) → white (FAQ) → white with a large mint rounded panel (CTA) → near-black footer.
- Services grid: 6 columns desktop, 20 cards → last row has only 2 cards, left-aligned (not centred).

## B. Section order (verified)
1. Header 2. Hero 3. Featured-in strip 4. Why us (3 stat cards) 5. Our services (20 cards) 6. How it works (dark, 3 phone cards) 7. Testimonials (two-row auto-scrolling marquee) 8. FAQ (20 accordion rows) 9. Closing CTA (mint panel with fanned phones) 10. Footer (dark).

## C. Navigation (verified)
Logo left (green wordmark). Right-aligned: Why us · Services ▾ · Cities ▾ · How it works · FAQs. Services dropdown lists all 20 services + "View all services →". Cities dropdown lists 11 cities + "View all cities →". Anchor links `#why-us`, `#how-it-works`, `#faqs`. Header is small (est. 56–64px high), text ~13–14px, very light and minimal.

## D. Typography (mandated)
League Spartan (headings, big numbers, card titles) + DM Sans (everything else). Headings are tight, bold/semibold, left-aligned with ~1.05 line-height, sentences end with full stops ("Book trusted house help."). Eyebrows are tiny, uppercase, letter-spaced, green.

## E. Colour
Emerald #05AC5F (eyebrows, icons, phone frames, badges accents) · Mint #DAF3E7 (stat cards, CTA panel, hero wash) · Pale green #D2ECDE (secondary) · Near-black #0C0C0C (How it works + footer) · Light grey #F9FAFC (Why us) · White. No other hues. Body greys are neutral.

## F. Spacing rhythm
Section vertical padding est. 96–128px desktop, 64–80px mobile. 8-pt scale. Headings sit ~16px above their paragraph and ~48–56px above their content grid.

## G. Imagery
- Hero: realistic cutout PNG of a smiling Pronto professional (green uniform, hands in namaste) — extremely high impact.
- Services: soft, consistent, miniature 3D-ish "diorama" product illustrations on white/pale cards — each one distinct but same lighting/angle/style.
- How it works: real app screenshots inside phone mockups, sitting on bright emerald rounded frames. Step 1 and Step 3 are *slideshows* of 3 screens each (live site); Step 2 is a single screen.
- Testimonials: no photos; coloured initial avatar only.
- Closing CTA: three phones fanned/overlapping, top-centre of the mint panel.

## H. Components
- **Stat cards:** mint, ~16px radius, small green circular icon, big League Spartan number with "+", small grey caption. (Live site count-ups from 0.)
- **Service cards:** white, 1px light border, ~20px radius, square illustration area, 12px label bottom-left, tiny arrow bottom-right.
- **Step cards:** emerald rounded visual frame (~24px radius) containing phone mockup cropped at the bottom; "STEP n" tiny green label; white bold title; grey-on-black description.
- **Testimonial cards:** white, light border, small radius, 5 green stars, ~13px text, initial avatar + name + locality. Two rows scroll in opposite/same direction as marquee.
- **FAQ rows:** white, light border, ~12px radius, ~52px tall, chevron right, centred ~760px column.

## I. Buttons & CTAs
Official black Google Play / App Store badges (images). Text action "Request Pronto in your locality" (small green underlined/text link). Rating row: 5 green stars + "4.5 from 42,700+ ratings". "Live in" row of city text chips + "+ 4 more cities".

## J. Design language
Calm, spacious, bright, trust-first. Almost no shadows, almost no gradients (only the hero mint wash). No glass, no blobs.

## K. Conversion strategy
Hero states value + two app badges immediately → social proof (rating, 500,000+ homes, live cities) → press credibility → three big numbers → catalogue proves breadth and flat pricing → 3 steps remove friction → reviews → FAQ handles safety/price/cancellation objections (heavily trust-oriented: background verification, Pronto Verified) → repeat the same CTA → footer SEO links (all services, all cities).

